Mobile portrait sense: compass works, arrow and label visible, toast shows. Good. But the toast at bottom overlaps the touch buttons ("SENSE/TORCH/RUN") and the stick. The toast is at bottom max(90px, safe+80) → y ~? In portrait, it appears above the buttons but overlaps the top of the buttons slightly. It is centered, width 80vw, and the buttons are at y734; the toast is at y ~? It looks like y 1400 (image 2x) → CSS 700, height ~50, ending 725, just above buttons 734. It's fine. It overlaps the joystick area? The stick is left, toast centered; slight. Acceptable.

Mobile portrait scare: the HUD remains visible (manual show, not startDeath), but we see the scare head cropped heavily in portrait. That's expected: the scare camera aspect is 390/844 = 0.46; fov 34 vertical, so the horizontal FOV is narrow, and the huge head is cropped to the center (nose, teeth). It's still scary but maybe too cropped; you see only part of the face. For portrait, we may want to pull the scare camera back or reduce head scale to fit more of the face. Since the game is mobile-friendly, the jumpscare should read on portrait too. Currently it shows the nose/eye/teeth close-up, which is arguably scary, but the face is unrecognizable. We can adapt the scare camera distance by aspect: if aspect < 1, pull the camera back (increase z) and/or reduce head scale. In `updateCameraAspect`, compute a zoom factor: `this.zoom = aspect < 1 ? 1.35 : 1` and use it in `lookAt`? Better: set `this.camera.position.z = 9.0 * (aspect < 1 ? 1.55 : 1)` and reduce fov? Or move head back at hold. Since the head position is animated in update, we can multiply the z by a factor. Simplest: in `updateCameraAspect`, set `this.portrait = aspect < 0.8`; then in update, use `const depth = this.portrait ? 1.5 : 1` and scale z distances around origin? The head z is in world and camera z 9. To pull back, increase camera z to 13 for portrait; then at same head z 2.5, distance 10.5, frame height 6.4 → head 60% (good). Also camera lookAt. FOV stays 34. This will show the whole face in portrait.

Implement:
```
this.camZ = aspect < 0.85 ? 13.5 : 9.0;
this.camera.position.z = this.camZ;
```
But update sets camera.position.x/y only, leaving z. Good. At 13.5, the head at hold 2.5 distance 11, frame 6.7, head ~3.2 → 48% height. Maybe 12.0 → distance 9.5, frame 5.8, head 55%. Use 12.0. At start z -2 → 14, frame 8.6, head 37%. Good. Use 12.2.

Also the scare head may be too bright/overexposed in the portrait screenshot: the left side is blown out cream/white due to the key light at 78 and ambient. On desktop it looked okay; the portrait crop is closer to the nose, so the key light blows it out. Pulling back will reduce exposure. Also reduce key intensity maybe 60.

