But this runs every frame and hides HUD during the repair final scare too (already hidden). It won't affect the peek (short). It makes the manual test pass and is robust. Add a helper `hideGameUIForScare` maybe just inline. However, on the scare → dead transition, retry shows HUD. Good. But be careful: `jumpscare.active` remains true for the peek (short) and we don't hide. Fine.

Add this in the animate loop before render:
```
if (jumpscare.active && !jumpscare.short) {
  hide($('hud')); $('hud').classList.remove('show');
  hide($('touch')); hide($('compass')); hide($('reticle'));
  $('subtitle').classList.remove('show');
}
```
Could hide HUD while the intro/repair scare is active, which is intended. Do it only once? Classes are idempotent. Fine.

Also hide `.hud-hint` on touch via CSS.

Also the title landscape shows the desktop control hints and "HEADPHONES RECOMMENDED" — on touch landscape, the title-controls should be hidden. Add to `@media (hover:none)`:
```
.title-controls{display:none}
.hud-hint{display:none}
```
But the title controls hidden via max-width only on portrait. On touch landscape, hide. Good. Also maybe hide the top-right headphones? That's fine.

